; external equivalence is unverified.","Protective exit/cancel signatures are explicitly reconstructed from incomplete legacy artifacts.","Composite results and statistical windows use the bounded artifact-defined model; legacy BB v1-v3 is reconstructed and external equivalence is unverified.","Technical-analysis overloads are a bounded artifact-derived model; missing historical signatures are explicitly reconstructed.","Loops use versioned documented availability and bounded artifact-defined execution; historical reconstructions and platform equivalence remain unverified.","Arrays use a bounded primitive-reference heap in v4-v6; historical reconstruction and external equivalence are unverified.","UTC environment and bar phases follow pinned artifact-defined rules; external platform equivalence is unverified.","Signal/event and weighted-window functions follow a bounded artifact-defined model; external platform equivalence is unverified.","Partial exits use an explicit bounded historical OHLC model; incomplete v1-v3 quantity signatures are reconstructed and external equivalence is unverified.","Pending entries use a bounded historical OHLC model; incomplete v1-v2 signatures are reconstructed and intrabar activation never implies a known tick path.","Lot accounting is a bounded historical reconstruction: v1 header and v1-v3 close-entry selection gaps are explicit; no external TradingView execution oracle was used.","Order groups use a bounded historical reconstruction: v1 signatures and incomplete v2 parameters are explicit; OCA transitions and net-order allocation are artifact-defined policies, not external TradingView equivalence.","Relative exits and trailing use explicit per-lot historical rules: v1/v2 signatures and early parameter precedence are reconstructed; v5 absolute priority and v6 earliest directional level follow the pinned migration decision. OHLC activation/ratchet timing is a bounded model, not external execution equivalence.","Economic orders freeze quantity at confirmed creation close, with explicit qty precedence and downward rounding only for derived quantities. This bounded creation-time policy deliberately differs from fill-time equity sizing; gaps change notional, not frozen units. Flat fees are charged on the first actual fill per order ID. Legacy names/early signatures are reconstructed; no external execution equivalence is claimed.","Static global risk rules v1-v6 use observed open, actual fills and confirmed close. Close-triggered liquidation waits for next open; known-price boundaries liquidate immediately with normal costs. UTC observed days, W/M bar periods and explicit early-version reconstruction; no tick-path or external execution equivalence.","Trade observations use the existing historical ledger: a closed trade is one allocated closed lot slice, open indices are current surviving entry order, closed indices are stable from zero. Profit and win/loss classification use allocated net P/L, open profit deducts remaining entry fees. These commission and early-version choices are explicit reconstructions, not external execution equivalence."],"implementation_profile_id":"openpine.historical-bars.1","implementation_sha256":"cfe2dd0d973532c215c85b4dca2e1f7a3ff89deefee39c5ef73b64ddac2dc5dd","language_version":1,"semantic_profile_id":"pine1.historical-core.1+openpine.language.v1.1+openpine.series.v1.1+openpine.functions.v1.1+openpine.requests.v1.6+openpine.strategy.v1.1+openpine.exits.v1.1+openpine.composite.v1.1+openpine.technical.v1.1+openpine.loops.v1.1+openpine.arrays.v1.1+openpine.environment.v1.1+openpine.signals.v1.1+openpine.partial-exits.v1.1+openpine.pending-entries.v1.1+openpine.lots.v1.1+openpine.order-groups.v1.1+openpine.trailing.v1.1+openpine.economics.v1.1+openpine.risk.v1.1+openpine.performance.v1.1","semantic_sha256":"3bf788e9fdb20bdc4cc64e0f291e68024afb63af07e61fcb9fc4cff29676ebcb","source_sha256":"0396d54a4c90c3de7afba67815b14093a3e5ab6ed85d284261b98b75e1a4aa5d","spec_lock_sha256":"